    "content": "<h2>Common Symptoms of Vitamin B12 Deficiency</h2>\n<p>Vitamin B12 deficiency can develop gradually, and the symptoms may vary from person to person. Common signs include:</p>\n<ul>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Causes & Risk Factors</h2>\n<p>Vitamin B12 deficiency can occur when the diet does not provide enough B12 or when the body cannot absorb it properly. People following a strict vegan diet, older adults, and those with certain digestive conditions may have a higher risk. Some medicines can also affect B12 absorption.</p>\n\n<h2>How Is Vitamin B12 Deficiency Diagnosed?</h2>\n<p>A healthcare professional may recommend blood tests when B12 deficiency is suspected. The results may be considered along with symptoms, diet, medical history, and other tests to understand the possible cause.</p>\n",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "id": "faq-1787980764905-1j62fvss1",
        "question": "What are the common symptoms of vitamin B12 deficiency?",
        "answer": "Common symptoms can include tiredness, weakness, pale skin, headaches, numbness or tingling, and a sore tongue. Some people may also experience problems with concentration."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-1787980765344-gt55adsc5",
        "question": "What causes vitamin B12 deficiency?",
        "answer": "It can result from not getting enough B12 in the diet or from problems absorbing the vitamin. Certain digestive conditions, age-related changes, and some medicines can increase the risk."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-1787980765624-fbhee9wkm",
        "question": "Which foods are rich in vitamin B12?",
        "answer": "Fish, meat, poultry, eggs, and dairy products are common sources. Some fortified cereals and plant-based foods also contain vitamin B12."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-1787980817969-fzhebdbjl",
        "question": "Can vegetarians and vegans become deficient in vitamin B12?",
        "answer": "People who avoid animal-based foods may have a higher risk because natural B12 is mainly found in animal products. Fortified foods or supplements may be useful when appropriate."
      }
    ],
    "reviewCycle": "12 months",
