    "introduction": "Iron deficiency anemia is a common disease which results due to the lack of iron in the body required for the formation of healthy red blood cells and hemoglobin. Because hemoglobin helps carry oxygen throughout the body, the lack of it may result in tiredness and exhaustion.\n\nThere are various causes of iron deficiency anemia, which include poor nutrition, blood loss, pregnancy, or malabsorption of iron.",
