    "imageAlt": "vitamin D deficiency",
    "disclaimerType": "clinical",
    "quickAnswer": "Vitamin D deficiency turns out to be more common than one would expect. It happens when there’s a lack of sun exposure or dietary intake of this vitamin. And the problem is that some people do not experience any symptoms at all, whereas others might face persistent muscle weakness, general body pains, or vague bone aches. In order to know whether you’re at risk, you’ll need just a single blood test. Luckily, everything can be put right by changing your diet a bit or taking supplements prescribed by your physician.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "id": "faq-1787735179732-2dayluegf",
        "question": "What are the symptoms of vitamin D deficiency?",
        "answer": "However, vitamin D deficiency might not result in any symptoms. Some of the possible symptoms include bone pain, muscle weakness and muscle pains. Deficiency to an advanced level affects bone health."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-1787735180451-vfs7xan1h",
        "question": "What causes vitamin D deficiency?",
        "answer": "Vitamin D deficiency can be caused by insufficient sun exposure, poor diet, health complications, difficulty in absorbing nutrients, age factors, and specific medications."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-1787735181027-heibbyxrq",
        "question": "Which foods are high in vitamin D?",
        "answer": "These include fatty fish like salmon and tuna. Another source of vitamin D is egg yolk as well as fortified foods containing vitamin D like certain types of milk, soy milk, and cereal."
      },
      {
        "id": "faq-1787735181515-wz04twkkj",
        "question": "Can vitamin D deficiency cause tiredness?",
        "answer": "Fatigue can result from vitamin D deficiency, although there are various reasons for fatigue. If you suffer from continuous fatigue that impacts your daily activities, it is recommended that you see a doctor instead of attributing the fatigue to vitamin D deficiency."
      }
    ],
