    "content": "<h2>Symptoms of Vitamin D Deficiency</h2>\n<p>Vitamin D deficiency does not always cause noticeable symptoms. When symptoms do appear, they can be mild and may be confused with other health problems. Common signs include:</p>\n<ul>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Causes & Risk Factors</h2>\n<p>Vitamin D deficiency can develop when the body does not get enough vitamin D from sunlight or food. Some people are more likely to have low levels because of their lifestyle, age, diet, or certain health conditions.</p>\n",
    "introduction": "The term “sunshine vitamin” is associated with vitamin D because it helps with the absorption of calcium in the body and ensures healthy bones and muscles. Although our body produces vitamin D with exposure to the sun, it is possible to increase the level of this substance by consuming particular foods or taking supplements.\n\nHowever, how do you know whether you have enough of this substance in the body? A lack of vitamin D does not always manifest itself with some symptoms, which means that you can easily miss it. If you want to know more about the signs, causes, and ways to increase the amount of this vitamin, then you came to the right place.",
