    "quickAnswer": "Imagine your liver to be a tireless machine that becomes overloaded at times. Overloading your liver with fat, which may happen due to unhealthy metabolism or drinking habits, leads to a condition where your liver becomes inefficient. The challenging thing about fatty liver disease is that it tends to be asymptomatic without any symptoms and is therefore detected unexpectedly during regular testing. The approach to treatment of fatty liver depends fully on its causes; however, you can change your lifestyle, eat better and get active.",
    "slug": "fatty-liver-disease-symptoms-causes-diagnosis-and-lifestyle-management",
