    "introduction": "Walk through any health food shop or scroll through social media and you'll encounter an impressive collection of foods that will apparently transform your health. Blueberries, acai, turmeric, goji berries, green tea, spirulina — the list keeps growing. The reality is more nuanced than the marketing suggests. Some of these foods do contain genuinely useful nutrients. But describing any single food as a \"superfood\" that will measurably improve your immune function is usually an overstatement. What the research consistently supports is the importance of nutritional patterns rather than individual ingredients.",
